sequenceDiagram
    participant Client as External Client
    participant Mux as cmux Multiplexer<br/>8000/TCP
    participant HTTP as HTTP Server<br/>(fasthttp)
    participant GRPC as gRPC Server<br/>(VllmEngine)
    participant Engine as vLLM Engine
    participant Sim as Simulator Core<br/>(Worker Queue)
    participant Render as vllm-render Sidecar<br/>8082/TCP
    participant KV as KV-Cache Subsystem
    participant ZMQ as ZMQ PUB Socket
    participant EPP as llm-d-router EPP<br/>(ZMQ SUB)

    rect rgb(230, 245, 255)
    Note over Client,HTTP: Flow 1: HTTP Inference (Streaming)
    Client->>Mux: POST /v1/chat/completions<br/>HTTP/1.1, Optional TLS 1.2+
    Mux->>HTTP: Route (HTTP/1.1 match)
    HTTP->>Engine: Parse & validate request
    Engine->>Sim: Submit to worker queue
    Sim->>Sim: Apply TTFT latency simulation
    loop Token Generation
        Sim->>Sim: Generate token (random/echo mode)<br/>Apply inter-token decode delay
        Sim-->>Engine: Token via Go channel
        Engine-->>HTTP: SSE event (data: ...)
        HTTP-->>Client: Streamed SSE response
    end
    end

    rect rgb(255, 243, 230)
    Note over Client,GRPC: Flow 2: gRPC Inference (Streaming)
    Client->>Mux: Generate RPC<br/>HTTP/2, Optional TLS 1.2+
    Mux->>GRPC: Route (HTTP/2 match)
    GRPC->>Engine: Parse protobuf request
    Engine->>Sim: Submit to worker queue
    Sim->>Sim: Apply latency simulation
    loop Token Generation
        Sim->>Sim: Generate token
        Sim-->>Engine: Token via Go channel
        Engine-->>GRPC: gRPC stream message
        GRPC-->>Client: Streamed protobuf response
    end
    end

    rect rgb(245, 230, 255)
    Note over Engine,ZMQ: Flow 3: KV-Cache Event Publication
    Engine->>KV: Block store/remove operation
    KV->>KV: Update in-memory block cache
    KV->>ZMQ: Serialize event (msgpack tagged union)
    ZMQ->>EPP: Publish event<br/>ZMQ TCP, No encryption
    end

    rect rgb(230, 255, 230)
    Note over Engine,Render: Flow 4: Tokenization via Render Sidecar
    Client->>Mux: POST /v1/chat/completions/render
    Mux->>HTTP: Route
    HTTP->>Engine: Render request
    Engine->>Render: POST /tokenize<br/>HTTP 8082/TCP localhost
    Render-->>Engine: Token IDs + count
    Engine-->>HTTP: Render response
    HTTP-->>Client: JSON response
    end
